{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30029 - PROTEIN:5781",
  "verbalization": "Cassialactone is implicated in the biological activity of A2780cisR through a multi-step pathway involving Microtubule-associated protein 1B. This protein is targeted by both 5-(2-Thienylethynyl)-2-thiophenemethanol and Amurensin, which in turn direct the activity toward A2780cisR. The evidence suggests that Cassialactone acts as a modulator of the signaling cascade initiated by these compounds, ultimately influencing the target protein A2780cisR. The consistent presence of Microtubule-associated protein 1B as a common intermediate across different targets implies a potential role in the cellular response to Cassialactone. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Cassialactone may interact with A2780cisR, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
